---
  import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

  <Layout
  title="This website — case study — Mike Trounce"
  description="How miketrounce.com got built: one clear job, done in Astro, without adding anything it doesn't need yet."
  >
  <div class="cs-page">
  <a href="/" class="back-link">&larr; Mike Trounce</a>

  <header class="cs-hero">
  <img src="/mike.jpg" alt="Mike Trounce" width="184" height="282" />
  <p class="cs-caption">Mike Trounce — miketrounce.com</p>
  </header>

  <span class="cs-label">Case study 2</span>
  <h1>This website</h1>
  <p class="cs-meta">Personal site &middot; Live</p>

  <p class="cs-standfirst">
  Not a client fix this time — this is the site you're reading now, and the general approach behind it: give it one clear job, build only what that job needs, and pick tools that don't box you in later.
  </p>

  <section>
  <h2>One job, done plainly</h2>
  <p>
  The site has a single job: say who I am, what I take off a founder's plate, and make it easy to get in touch. Everything on it serves that — no blog to maintain, no CMS to configure, nothing that exists because a website "should" have it.
  </p>
  <p>
  That's the same principle behind the client work described elsewhere on this site: notice what's actually needed, build that, and stop.
  </p>

  <details class="tech-detail" id="technical">
  <summary>Technical detail: why Astro</summary>
  <p>
  The site is built in <a href="https://astro.build" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Astro</a>, a framework built for content-first sites. Pages ship as plain HTML with very little JavaScript, so it's fast by default and simple to reason about — a good fit for a handful of pages like this one.
  </p>
  <p>
  Astro isn't limited to static output, though. It can render pages on request and connect to a database — Postgres, for instance — if the site ever needed one: a contact form that stores submissions, a small admin area, anything with real data behind it. Nothing here needs that yet, but the option's there without a rebuild.
</p>
<p>
It's hosted on Cloudflare Pages, deployed straight from the <code>main</code> branch of the site's GitHub repo — push a commit, the site updates.
</p>
</details>
</section>

<p class="cs-foot">
<a href="/">&larr; Mike Trounce</a>
</p>
</div>
</Layout>

<style>
.cs-page {
max-width: 680px;
margin: 0 auto;
padding: 4rem 1.5rem 6rem;
color: var(--ink);
}

.back-link {
display: inline-block;
margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
color: var(--ink-soft);
text-decoration: none;
font-size: 0.9rem;
}
.back-link:hover { color: var(--accent); }

.cs-hero img {
display: block;
width: 100%;
max-width: 184px;
height: auto;
border-radius: 20px;
background: var(--bg-raised);
box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(var(--shadow) / 0.05), 0 18px 34px -18px rgba(var(--shadow) / 0.4);
}
.cs-caption {
margin: 0.7rem 0 0;
font-size: 0.85rem;
color: var(--ink-faint);
}

.cs-label {
display: inline-block;
margin-top: 2.5rem;
font-size: 0.82rem;
font-weight: 600;
letter-spacing: 0.02em;
text-transform: uppercase;
color: var(--ink-soft);
padding-bottom: 6px;
border-bottom: 2px solid var(--illus-a);
}

h1 { margin: 0.75rem 0 0.25rem; }

.cs-meta {
margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
color: var(--ink-soft);
font-size: 0.85rem;
text-transform: uppercase;
letter-spacing: 0.02em;
}

.cs-standfirst {
font-size: 1.15rem;
color: var(--ink-soft);
margin: 0 0 2rem;
}

section h2 {
font-size: 1.3rem;
margin: 3rem 0 0.75rem;
}
section p {
margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
color: var(--ink-soft);
}
section p a { color: var(--accent); }

.tech-detail {
margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
background: var(--bg-raised);
border: 1px solid var(--illus-a);
border-radius: 12px;
padding: 0.9rem 1.2rem;
}
.tech-detail summary {
cursor: pointer;
font-size: 0.82rem;
font-weight: 600;
text-transform: uppercase;
letter-spacing: 0.02em;
color: var(--ink-soft);
}
.tech-detail[open] summary {
margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
}
.tech-detail p {
margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
color: var(--ink-soft);
font-size: 0.95rem;
}
.tech-detail p:last-child {
margin-bottom: 0;
}
.tech-detail code {
background: var(--illus-b);
padding: 0.1rem 0.35rem;
border-radius: 4px;
font-size: 0.85em;
}
.tech-detail a { color: var(--accent); }

.cs-foot {
margin-top: 3rem;
font-size: 0.9rem;
color: var(--ink-faint);
}
.cs-foot a {
color: var(--ink-soft);
text-decoration: none;
}
</style>
